@startuml proposalEditorDataFlow
' Proposal editor: data flow from creating a proposal to saving, refreshing and submitting it.
' Lifelines are where the data is held; arrows are how it moves and is transformed.

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEFECE

actor User
participant "formState\n(ProposalFormInput)" as Form
database "localStorage\n(backup)" as Backup
database "backend\n(proposal PDM)" as Backend

== Create ==

User -> Form : proposal type and title, Create
Form -> Backend : toPdm(values), POST

alt created
  Backend --> Form : new proposal\nfromPdm(pdm), reset form
else POST failed
  Form --> User : error message\n(stays on the Title page)
end

== Editing ==

User -> Form : user input
note over Form
  RHF validates with ProposalSubmitSchema
end note
Form -> Backup : backup ProposalFormInput (debounced)

== Save ==

User -> Form : leaves the editor, Save, or 30 s timer
Form -> Backup : backup ProposalFormInput\n(immediately, no debounce)

alt ProposalDraftSchema.safeParse(getValues()) OK
  Form -> Backend : toPdm(values), PUT
  Form -> Backup : mark backup as saved
else parse or PUT failed
  Form --> User : "not saved" message\n(leaving the editor is never blocked)
end

== Refresh ==

User -> Form : page refresh
Backup --> Form : ID of the proposal being edited
Form -> Backend : GET

alt fetched
  Backend --> Form : proposal\nfromPdm(pdm), reset form
  opt backup has unsaved changes
    Backup --> Form : apply ProposalFormInput on top
  end
else fetch failed
  Form --> User : "Something went wrong retrieving\nproposal with ID <prsl_id>"
end

... more input and saves ...

== Submit ==

User -> Form : Submit
note over Form
  handleSubmit validates every field
  with ProposalSubmitSchema
end note

alt issues
  Form --> User : validation issue summary (pop-up)
else valid
  Form -> Backend : toPdm(values) + submitted_by, PUT
  note over Backend
    For now, backend sets proposal status
    based on submitted_by field; a future
    feature will likely add a separate
    submit endpoint
  end note
  Form -> Backup : clear backup
end

@enduml
